IN-PERSON NETWORKING: MAKING IT CONCRETE
Joshua was direct about this: face-to-face changes the conviction of the person in front of you.
Here is how to make it a system rather than an occasional thing.
• Search Meetup, LinkedIn Events, Hasgeek, and Google for 'Bangalore tech meetup' or
'Bangalore data engineering' or 'Bangalore distributed systems' monthly. Commit to attending
2 per month.
• Uber Bengaluru almost certainly hosts or participates in external events. Your security badge
does not follow you out the door but your Uber affiliation does. Use it to open conversations.
• Your goal at every event is not to find a job. It is to have 3 interesting technical conversations.
Nothing more. The job part follows over subsequent interactions.
• When you meet someone interesting, connect on LinkedIn within 24 hours with a note
referencing something specific from your conversation. That is your anchor for future
outreach.
• For global opportunities: search LinkedIn for Indians at your target European or APAC
companies. Message them specifically about their relocation experience and what the
sponsorship process looked like. This research saves months of guessing.

