NAVIGATING GLOBAL OPPORTUNITIES
For roles outside India, the research and networking approach is slightly different. Here is the
framework Joshua recommended:
• Make a short list of 5 target countries or markets first: do not try to optimize for 'anywhere
global' all at once. Choose regions where your tech stack is in demand: UK, Netherlands,
Germany, Singapore, and Canada are solid options for distributed systems and data platform
engineers.
• For each market, identify 3 to 5 companies actively hiring senior backend or data platform
engineers. Use LinkedIn Jobs filtered by location and then look at the hiring team.
• Find Indians who have made this move. Search LinkedIn for '[Company] [Senior Engineer]
India' or browse IIITD alumni groups for people at your target companies. Their first-hand
experience on sponsorship, timelines, and culture will save you months.
• Avoid startups in Europe if visa sponsorship is required. European regulatory requirements
make sponsorship costly for early-stage companies. Mid-size to large product companies are
your best bets.
• Ask specifically: does this company have a history of sponsoring Indian engineers at the senior
level? Have they done it in the last 12 months? If yes, they know the process and will move
faster.
• Your GitHub and patent (rotary Braille device, Patent No. 201911002013) are legitimately
impressive and differentiate you globally. Lead with these in your outreach to international
companies: innovation track record travels well.

